Instruments that are garbage collected without having been closed now emit a ``ResourceWarning``
(like unclosed files) when the garbage collector closes them. Garbage collection only closes
instruments on a best effort basis, at an arbitrary later point in time, so instruments should
always be closed explicitly, e.g. with ``close`` or ``Instrument.close_all``.
Python hides ``ResourceWarning`` by default, but it is shown e.g. by pytest and in Python's
development mode. Test suites that turn warnings into errors report it as an exception ignored in
``Instrument.__del__``. Instruments that fail to initialize are still closed without a warning.
